# Design System Rules

This project uses CSS custom properties (variables) for consistent styling.
All design decisions should use these tokens instead of hardcoded values.

## File Reference
@app/globals.css

## Spacing System

Use the spacing scale (8px base unit) for all margins, padding, and gaps:

| Token         | Value | Usage |
|---------------|-------|-------|
| `--space-xs`  | 8px   | Component internal padding, minimal gaps |
| `--space-sm`  | 16px  | Related content groupings (buttons, form fields) |
| `--space-md`  | 24px  | Sub-section separations |
| `--space-lg`  | 32px  | Section content gaps |
| `--space-xl`  | 48px  | Major section divisions |
| `--space-2xl` | 64px  | Top-level container gaps |

### Rules
- NEVER use hardcoded pixel values for spacing (e.g., `padding: 12px`)
- Use CSS variables: `padding: var(--space-sm)`
- In Tailwind, use: `p-[var(--space-sm)]` or the custom spacing classes

## Typography Scale

Use the typography scale for all font sizes:

| Token         | Value     | Usage |
|---------------|-----------|-------|
| `--text-xs`   | 0.75rem   | Fine print, labels |
| `--text-sm`   | 0.875rem  | Secondary text, captions |
| `--text-base` | 1rem      | Body text (default) |
| `--text-lg`   | 1.125rem  | Emphasized body text |
| `--text-xl`   | 1.25rem   | Subheadings |
| `--text-2xl`  | 1.5rem    | Section headings |
| `--text-3xl`  | 2rem      | Page headings |

### Rules
- Use rem-based font sizes from the scale
- Avoid hardcoded pixel values for font-size

## Color System

This project supports multiple themes (BTTF, Matrix). Use semantic color variables:

### Background Colors
- `--bg-main` - Main background
- `--bg-panel` - Panel/card backgrounds
- `--bg-panel-header` - Panel header backgrounds

### Text Colors
- `--text-main` - Primary text
- `--text-muted` - Secondary/dimmed text
- `--text-accent-1` - Input panel accent (red in BTTF)
- `--text-accent-2` - Tree panel accent (green in BTTF)
- `--text-accent-3` - Preview panel accent (yellow in BTTF)

### Border Colors
- `--border-main` - Default borders
- `--border-accent-1/2/3` - Accent borders matching text colors

### Rules
- NEVER hardcode colors like `#ff0000` or `red`
- Use theme-aware variables: `color: var(--text-main)`
- For Tailwind: `text-[var(--text-main)]` or `bg-[var(--bg-panel)]`

## Border Radius

| Token          | Value   | Usage |
|----------------|---------|-------|
| `--radius-sm`  | 4px     | Small elements (buttons, inputs) |
| `--radius-md`  | 8px     | Cards, panels |
| `--radius-lg`  | 16px    | Large containers |
| `--radius-full`| 9999px  | Circular elements |

## Transitions

| Token              | Value  | Usage |
|--------------------|--------|-------|
| `--duration-fast`  | 0.15s  | Micro-interactions (hover, focus) |
| `--duration-normal`| 0.3s   | Standard transitions |
| `--duration-slow`  | 0.5s   | Larger animations |

### Example
```css
transition: all var(--duration-normal) var(--ease-out);
```

## Common Patterns

### Panel Styling
```tsx
<div className="bg-[var(--bg-panel)] border border-[var(--border-main)] rounded-[var(--radius-md)]">
```

### Button Styling
Use the `.theme-button` class for consistent button styling across themes.

### Digital Text Effect
Use the `.digital-text` class for the retro LCD/LED text effect.
